Every time I use the quantile function I really feel it needs to use the names provided to the `probs` argument. So I can do `quantile(x, probs = c(low = 0.05, mid = 0.5, high = 0.95))`  or similar. It should be a relatively straightforward addition, something like this:

```quantile <- function(
  x,
  probs = seq(0, 1, 0.25),
  na.rm = FALSE,
  names = TRUE,
  type = 7,
  digits = 7,
  fuzz = if (type == 7L) 0 else 4 * .Machine$double.eps,
  ...
) {
  q <- stats::quantile(x, probs, na.rm, names, type, digits, fuzz, ...)
  if (!names) {
    return(q)
  }

  if (is.null(names(probs))) {
    return(q)
  }

  names(q) <- ifelse(names(probs) == "", names(q), names(probs))
  q
}```
Would this be a good topic for r-dev you think?

